course: dictionary
lesson: 13732
title: Intensely
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word intensely means very strongly, deeply or extremely. It tells you how much something happens. «She stared intensely at the painting» means she looked very hard and did not look away.
explain: Intensely boosts the word next to it. «The sun was intensely hot» means the sun was extremely hot, not just warm. To check, swap in very strongly or extremely and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Intensely can also show feeling. «He felt intensely sad when his dog ran away» tells you the sadness was deep. Use the other words in the sentence to work out how strong the feeling is.
fact: Intensely is an adverb, so it tells you how strongly something happens or how something is.
fact: «Intensely» means very strongly, deeply or extremely.
fact: «She stared intensely» means she looked with deep concentration.
fact: «The sun was intensely hot» means the sun was extremely hot.
fact: A good check is to swap in very strongly or extremely and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The sun was intensely hot at noon.» What does intensely mean here? | Quietly | Rarely | *Extremely | Slightly
exercise: «She stared intensely at the painting.» What does stared intensely suggest? | She looked only for a second | She laughed loudly at it | She closed her eyes and fell asleep | *She looked very hard and did not look away
exercise: Which word in «The lamp gave an intensely bright light.» means very strongly? | light | gave | lamp | *intensely
test: «The cave was intensely dark, so we used a torch.» What does intensely mean? | *Extremely | A little | Happily
test: Which sentence uses intensely to mean deeply? | «We walked to school after lunch.» | «The bus was yellow.» | *«She felt intensely proud of her team.»
exam: Which word could replace intensely in «The water was intensely cold» and keep the same meaning? | Once | Quickly | Under | *Extremely
